ere in the first  part we extract the information we need  about the trace and the span from the  context note that there are two steps  here we get the span from the request  context then extract its span context  and finally use that to get the trace ID  and span ID in the second part we use  that information to construct our log  entry we write the log payload and add  the trace and span ID information to it  here's what our log entry it looks like  when it's written to cloud logging  notice that it contained information by  the trace and span  finally when we go to trace we can see  that our trace now includes log entries  we can use them to better understand  exactly what's happening if one of the  spans in the trace shows a latency issue  using open telemetry to connect traces  with logs is a great way to improve the  observer ability of our service and make  latency issues much easier to debug  that's it for this episode thank you for  watching and come back soon for more  this is a stack Doctor stay healthy out  there  [Music]
 

